l=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" pointer-events=\"none\">Biology</text>\n<text x=\"309.7\" y=\"166.8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11.2\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" pointer-events=\"none\">Calculus</text>\n<text x=\"456.0\" y=\"305.8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11.2\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" pointer-events=\"none\">Data Visualization</text>\n<text x=\"95.0\" y=\"389.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11.2\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" pointer-events=\"none\">Literature</text>\n<text x=\"261.8\" y=\"157.4\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11.2\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" pointer-events=\"none\">Chemistry</text>\n<g class=\"ec-legend\" transform=\"translate(681.9 12.4) scale(0.9884)\"><text x=\"0.0\" y=\"12.0\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\">slot</text><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"29.0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#4e79a7\" stroke=\"#365474\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\"/><text x=\"22.0\" y=\"29.0\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\">0</text><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"46.0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#f28e2c\" stroke=\"#a9631e\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\"/><text x=\"22.0\" y=\"46.0\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\">1</text><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"63.0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#e15759\" stroke=\"#9d3c3e\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\"/><text x=\"22.0\" y=\"63.0\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\">2</text><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"80.0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#76b7b2\" stroke=\"#52807c\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\"/><text x=\"22.0\" y=\"80.0\" font-family=\"-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"var(--ect-8a2de1d4)\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\">3</text></g>\n</svg>\n<div id=\"ec-tooltip-1\" style=\"\n  display:none;position:absolute;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;\n  font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;font-size:12px;pointer-events:none;\n  background:var(--ect-57425a7e);color:var(--ect-21ade003);\n  box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.18);max-width:min(260px,100%);box-sizing:border-box;\n  z-index:999;line-height:1.4;overflow-wrap:anywhere;\n\"></div>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var tip=document.currentScript.parentElement.querySelector('#ec-tooltip-1');\n  var svg=document.currentScript.parentElement.querySelector('svg');\n  if(!svg||!tip) return;\n  // Next to the pointer but inside the plot (flipped to the pointer's left near the right edge),\n  // since anything past its edges is clipped, and scrolls, in a notebook or Quarto cell\n  function place(ev){\n    var r=svg.getBoundingClientRect();\n    var x=ev.clientX-r.left+12,y=ev.clientY-r.top-10;\n    if(x+tip.offsetWidth>r.width) x=ev.clientX-r.left-12-tip.offsetWidth;\n    tip.style.left=Math.max(0,Math.min(x,r.width-tip.offsetWidth))+'px';\n    tip.style.top=Math.max(0,Math.min(y,r.height-tip.offsetHeight))+'px';\n  }\n  function show(el,ev){\n    var raw=el.getAttribute('data-attrs');\n    if(!raw) return;\n    try{var d=JSON.parse(raw)}catch(e){return}\n    var h='';\n    for(var k in d){\n      var v=d[k];\n      if(Array.isArray(v)) v=v.join(', ');\n      h+='<div><b>'+k+'</b>: '+v+'</div>';\n    }\n    if(!h) return;\n    tip.innerHTML=h;tip.style.display='block';\n    place(ev);\n  }\n  svg.addEventListener('mouseover',function(ev){\n    var t=ev.target;\n    if(t.hasAttribute('data-node')||t.hasAttribute('data-edge')) show(t,ev);\n  });\n  svg.addEventListener('mousemove',function(ev){\n    if(tip.style.display==='block') place(ev);\n  });\n  svg.addEventListener('mouseout',function(ev){\n    var t=ev.target;\n    if(t.hasAttribute('data-node')||t.hasAttribute('data-edge'))\n      tip.style.display='none';\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</div></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe timetable uses four slots. Counting the exams and students in each:\n\n::: {#783c3a14 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport polars as pl\n\n(\n    exams.get_node_df()\n    .group_by(\"slot\")\n    .agg(pl.len().alias(\"exams\"), pl.col(\"students\").sum())\n    .sort(\"slot\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>slot</th><th>exams</th><th>students</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>u32</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>205</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>7</td><td>490</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>245</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>95</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe slots are uneven: half the exams fall in slot 1, and Chemistry has slot 3 to itself.\nA coloring only promises that no two neighbors share a color, not that the colors are\nbalanced.\n\n### Four slots is the fewest possible\n\nCalculus, Physics, Chemistry and Biology all share students with one another, so each of\nthem needs its own slot. They are the largest clique in the network:\n\n::: {#ed0f0759 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\n(\n    exams.clique_number(),\n    [exams.get_label_from_id(n) for n in exams.maximum_clique()],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n(4, ['Calculus', 'Physics', 'Chemistry', 'Biology'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The order matters\n\nA greedy coloring gives each course the lowest slot its neighbors leave free, so the order\nin which it takes the courses decides how many slots it ends up with. The default,\n`\"largest_first\"`, needs a fifth:\n\n::: {#d1c048c1 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\n{\n    strategy: len(set(exams.greedy_color(strategy=strategy).values()))\n    for strategy in [\"largest_first\", \"smallest_last\", \"dsatur\"]\n}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```\n{'largest_first': 5, 'smallest_last': 4, 'dsatur': 4}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe fifth slot goes to Databases. By the time `\"largest_first\"` reaches it, its four\nneighbors are in four different slots, 0 to 3:\n\n::: {#9c0f44c2 .cell execution_count=6}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfirst = exams.greedy_color()\nlabel = exams.get_label_from_id\ndatabases = exams.get_id_from_label(\"Databases\")\n\nneighbors = {label(n): first[n] for n in exams.get_neighbors(databases)}\nneighbors, first[databases]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=6}\n```\n({'Statistics': 3, 'Psychology': 1, 'Programming': 2, 'Data Visualization': 0},\n 4)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWith `interchange=True`, it would first try to free a slot by swapping two slots along a\nchain of courses, and here that brings it down to four:\n\n::: {#36c5dd49 .cell execution_count=7}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nlen(set(exams.greedy_color(interchange=True).values()))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=7}\n```\n4\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNo strategy is best on every graph, so on a hard instance it's worth running several and\nkeeping the coloring with the fewest colors. `is_valid_coloring()` checks a coloring from\nany source.\n\n",
